{"name":"Lizard Breath","hex":"#edbb32","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lizard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any reptile of the order Squamata that is not a snake or mosasaur—typically characterised by a rounded torso, a short neck with an elevated head, a long tail and four limbs, although some species are legless.","Lizard skin, the skin of these reptiles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lizard"},{"term":"breath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process of breathing.","A single act of breathing in or out; a breathing of air."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["voiceless, surd; contrasting with voice (breath sounds, voice sounds)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lizard","blocks":[{"text":"Lizard is the common name used for all squamate reptiles that are not snakes, encompassing over 7,000 species. They have a cosmopolitan distribution, ranging across all continents except Antarctica, as well as most oceanic island chains. Extant lizard species vary in size from the 13.5 mm (0.53 in) nano-chameleon and the 14–18 mm (0.55–0.71 in) Jaragua dwarf gecko to the 3-meter-long Komodo dragon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Hemidactylus_platyurus_%28Flat-tailed_House_Gecko%29_on_white_background%2C_focus_stacking.jpg/330px-Hemidactylus_platyurus_%28Flat-tailed_House_Gecko%29_on_white_background%2C_focus_stacking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizard","wikidata":"Q15879"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Hemidactylus_platyurus_%28Flat-tailed_House_Gecko%29_on_white_background%2C_focus_stacking.jpg/500px-Hemidactylus_platyurus_%28Flat-tailed_House_Gecko%29_on_white_background%2C_focus_stacking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb